# Frontend i18n (en / si)

## Package

`@webonone/i18n` owns plumbing only: `createAppI18n`, `common` JSON (`en`/`si`), `webonone.locale` storage, `lng` query helpers, `normalizeLocale`.

- Default + fallback: **`en`**
- Supported: **`en`**, **`si`**
- Do **not** put feature copy in the package — only reusable chrome (`Save`, `Cancel`, …)

## Per service

1. `frontend/src/i18n/index.ts` — `createAppI18n({ resources, ns })` merging common + local packs
2. `frontend/src/locales/{en,si}/*.json` — feature namespaces
3. Call init from `main.tsx` before render
4. Wire `AppShell` `locale` / `onLocaleChange` / `headerLabels` via `changeAppLocale`
5. Persist preference with Identity `PATCH /auth/me` `{ locale }` when authenticated
6. Relay `lng` with theme on redirects/embeds (`relayLocaleQueryParams` / `LOCALE_QUERY`)

## UI Kit

Primitives stay locale-agnostic — pass `t(...)` as props. `AppHeader` accepts language menu props only; no i18n runtime inside the kit.

## Keys

| Put in | Examples |
|--------|----------|
| `common:*` | Save, Cancel, Edit, Delete, Loading |
| Service `ns:*` | `calendar.createEvent`, `auth.loginTitle` |

Use `useTranslation('ns')` / `t('common:save')`. Missing `si` keys fall back to English.

## Date display

User-visible dates use **`Oct 10, 2026`** (short month, numeric day, comma, year) via shared `DISPLAY_DATE_OPTIONS` and `INTL_LOCALE_TAGS` — see [date-display-format.mdc](date-display-format.mdc) and [date-display skill](../skills/date-display/SKILL.md). Pass `i18n.language` into format helpers; do not hard-code `en-US` in feature code.

## Verification

```bash
npm run build:i18n
npm run type-check -w @webonone/<service>-frontend
```
